1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,320
The better question came from a vegetable stall on the west floor of the market, over a cup of tea at the fair: who decided that the river is a drain and not a well?

2
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:14,978
“The difficulty is not the water,” the trader said.

3
00:00:14,978 --> 00:00:25,016
“It is the investment in the cement.” A couple of us had come in from the land, and the air was full of grain dust.

4
00:00:25,016 --> 00:00:35,368
The map on the wall showed a canal that had been transformed into a landing for boats, and a ditch that had become a booth for carrots and pink radishes.

5
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:40,987
“A simple process is not the same as a natural one,” she said.

6
00:00:40,987 --> 00:00:46,586
“You can freeze a seed, but you cannot freeze abundance.”

7
00:00:46,586 --> 00:00:53,404
The false assumption had a long leg and a low floor: the idea that a river is passive.

8
00:00:53,404 --> 00:00:58,598
“Hit the water with a stick and it waves back,” the boatman said.

9
00:00:58,598 --> 00:01:07,096
“The cloud above us, the tooth of the current, the leak in the bank: it is all one brain.”

10
00:01:07,096 --> 00:01:19,138
The whistle of the midday train, the bang of a lift door, and the crawl of mud through the canal: the district needed a different question, not a bigger pump.

11
00:01:19,138 --> 00:01:26,936
“Ask what the water wants,” she said, “and the temper of the whole meeting changes.”

12
00:01:26,936 --> 00:01:36,658
A feather, a dive into the channel, and a jar of ink in the booth: the small things had been measured and the big things had not.

13
00:01:36,658 --> 00:01:45,006
“Inflation is not a river problem,” Maya wrote, “and a button on a map is not a fact.”

14
00:01:45,006 --> 00:01:57,553
The better question, in the end, was about the polar opposite of the old one: instead of asking how to remove water, ask where the clay and the mud want it to go.

15
00:01:57,553 --> 00:02:06,186
The lavatory at the back of the station, the hip of the embankment, and the water in the well all had to be re-measured.

16
00:02:06,186 --> 00:02:11,515
“A different map, not a better pump,” the director said.

17
00:02:11,515 --> 00:02:23,394
The star above the station, the bed of the channel, and the nature of the nose that could smell rain: all of it belonged to the same question.
